From e53d0f1bf43f609e2bfe7f827484ed89df0f0505 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yiyu Zhou <yiyu@yiyuzhou.io>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 13:25:53 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Keep ready frames when ThreadedDecoder reports an error

decode_nal_buffered gathered ready frames and then returned Err in two
places, losing them: a worker's macroblock error from an earlier
picture, and a slice header error on a slice that starts a new picture.
Frames that are ready are now returned, and the error is reported on a
later call, the first one kept as before. flush still clears a pending
error, and a failed IDR slice header still does not bump the GOP.

The regression test cuts one slice NAL in the middle of a stream at
every length from 0 to 23 bytes, for 1 to 3 threads and three reorder
depths, and checks that every other picture is output.

Assisted-by: Claude Code (Claude Sonnet 5.5)
